I edited `out/w4-B.workflow.json` in place. It still loads with python3, and the changed close_call hook code compiles. Nothing was re-run, so none of these fixes has been tested yet. The start code node and the account post_process_code are unchanged.

- **Elena, both `create_promise` errors "unknown product_id" (`cc_6604`):** fixed. The agent built an id from the card digits instead of using the one the account tool returned. The ACCOUNT section of the negotiate prompt now says to use only a `product_id` shown in the account list, copied exactly, never one built from the card digits or product name. If a tool answers "unknown product_id", the agent retries with the exact id from that list.
- **Lena, `close_call` before `transfer_to_agent`, plus the "already closed" errors after it:** fixed. The check is right, because brief rule 32 (hardship) comes before rule 41 (new payment plan). The hardship rule now says that when job loss and a plan request come together, the agent offers only the support team. If the customer accepts, it calls `transfer_to_agent` (support) first, then `close_call`, with no notes. In all 5 copies of the CLOSING text, I added an ORDER rule: any note or transfer that is due comes first, `close_call` is always the last tool, and no tool is called after it succeeds.
- **Lena, `close_call` called 4 times:** fixed. That ORDER rule covers it. I also changed one line in the `close_call` result hook: an "already closed" error now tells the agent to call no more tools, instead of "try close_call once more".
- **Lena, `add_note` "already closed":** fixed. This came from the same wrong order. The hardship rule now says no notes after a transfer.
- **Priya, both calls, `add_note` "already closed" after `close_call`:** fixed. The check is right, because brief B rule 8 requires a note for every product without a promise. The "I already paid" rule now says to call `add_note` with reason `paid` and the product's id before `close_call`, and the ORDER rule backs this up.
- **Priya, `close_call` called 4 times and not last:** fixed by the ORDER rule and the hook change above.

